WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.650
Lab 2 runs on your own test instance.

2
00:00:02.650 --> 00:00:04.625
It hasn't been run by the authors.

3
00:00:04.625 --> 00:00:08.763
You need a test SQL Server instance,
never production, PowerShell 7 with

4
00:00:08.763 --> 00:00:12.700
the SQL Server module, and read
permissions granted for the lab only.

5
00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:13.950
Never sysadmin.

6
00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:16.638
Check the reading login's
own permissions first.

7
00:00:16.638 --> 00:00:20.974
Then export a SELECT-only audit snapshot,
and compare its login count with one

8
00:00:20.974 --> 00:00:25.312
the instance's administrator trusts: a
short list means a missing permission.

9
00:00:25.312 --> 00:00:26.337
Then audit it.

10
00:00:26.337 --> 00:00:28.224
Nothing on the instance changes.

11
00:00:28.224 --> 00:00:30.355
To back it out, delete the audit run,

12
00:00:30.355 --> 00:00:33.550
and have the administrator
remove the lab's grants.

13
00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:36.720
Keep the snapshot if you
go on to Module 3's Lab 2.
